# alfred runtime identity (canonical, fixed): user alfred UID 104,
# primary group alfred GID 104. Required by the shipped service units
# (alfred.service User=alfred, alfred.initd command_user alfred:alfred).
# The daemon retains only CAP_NET_ADMIN/CAP_NET_RAW across its setuid
# drop (file caps on the binary for OpenRC, ambient caps for systemd).
# UID 104 sits in the preferred 0..199 packaged range - never reuse it
# for another identity. No state directory: the unix socket lives under
# /run/alfred, provided per-boot by the service runtimes.
user alfred 104 alfred /var/empty /sbin/nologin
group alfred 104
